0 17 294 [
[(Here we listen to "pd-dsp-started" to receive a bang \050automatically)]
[(sent when DSP is started in Pd\051 to get the sample rate when DSP)]
[(starts. This also works whenever the sample rate may change when)]
[(the audio is running. This is useful when designing filters whose)]
[(coefficients usually have to be updated when the sample rate)]
[(changes. For more on this and other messages sent to and from Pd,)]
[(see [pd-messages].)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 17 362 [
[(When sent a "bang" message, [samplerate~] outputs the current audio)]
[(sample rate. If called within a subwindow that is up/down-sampled,)]
[(the sample rate of signals within that subwindow are reported \050see)]
[([pd resampling] subpatch below\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
